Subject: [LOCAL 6.6] Correct module namespace and declare A733 firmware

Linux 6.6 MODULE_IMPORT_NS stringifies its argument. Passing a string literal
produces import_ns="DMA_BUF" including quote characters in .modinfo. Use the
6.6 token form. Also expose the A733 firmware filename to packaging tools;
runtime firmware selection already uses the hardware BVNC.

This patch targets the pinned 6.6 backport, not a current upstream kernel.

--- a/pvr_drv.c
+++ b/pvr_drv.c
@@ -1559,6 +1559,7 @@
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Imagination Technologies Ltd.");
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION(PVR_DRIVER_DESC);
 MODULE_LICENSE("Dual MIT/GPL");
-MODULE_IMPORT_NS("DMA_BUF");
+MODULE_IMPORT_NS(DMA_BUF);
 MODULE_FIRMWARE("powervr/rogue_33.15.11.3_v1.fw");
 MODULE_FIRMWARE("powervr/rogue_36.53.104.796_v1.fw");
+MODULE_FIRMWARE("powervr/rogue_36.56.104.183_v1.fw");
